# LEGACY local working directories. Nothing defaults here any more (2026-09-23): a reader's
# mirror and its output now land OUTSIDE `evals/faithfulness/`, because Modal mounts this tree into
# every image build and a write under it kills any launch racing the hash. See
# `precompute/common.py`'s `mirror_dir` / `out_dir`, enforced by
# `unit_smoke.check_no_reader_default_under_the_mount`. They stay ignored because a checkout made
# before that commit still has them, full of fetched bytes.
#
# `faithfulness/` is NOT ignored (2026-09-21). It was, on the reasoning that everything under
# results/ is reproducible from the volume -- but eval 1's faithfulness output IS the paper's
# numbers, and a number the paper cites has to be in the history, diffable, and readable without
# $51 of GPU and a Modal token. So `results/faithfulness/` is committed -- as are `ood/`,
# `patchscopes/` and `tierb/` -- and each is written by NAMING it, `--out results/faithfulness`,
# at a moment the operator chose. That is exactly what a default cannot be.
data/
out/
